      "content": "the problem with going to the regulators or a manager is that they're all part of the same local network. if the system is rigged to liquidate certain people, reporting it to the people who run the system is just gonna tip them off that i'm onto them. i need more proactive stuff. like, are there ways to mask my transaction patterns or move funds in a way that bypasses their \"monitoring\" so they can't keep flagging my stuff? i need to stay one step ahead of their automation.",
